        "title": "Epideictic Rhetoric",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Epideictic rhetoric is the genre of praise and blame — the rhetoric of ceremonies, memorials, commemorations, and celebrations. It was the least studied of the three classical genres (Aristotle devoted less space to it than to deliberative or forensic) but it is the most frequent genre in professional and civic life. Every eulogy, commencement address, award presentation, team celebration, and organizational All-Hands operates in the epideictic mode."
